// `s.localeCompare(t)` where the code reads characters apart (std/lang/string/collate.velt):
// - strings that go on after a supplementary character (a 4-byte UTF-8 one);
// - combining marks against the accents of precomposed letters (`"eé"` vs `"e\u0301e"`), and before
//   and after characters outside the table;
// - the code points at the edges of each range the code treats apart (UTF-8 lengths, plane 16,
//   the table's blocks, the combining marks, Hangul, kana with its extension, Han with the
//   supplementary range), each against probes (printed as one sign per probe, in PROBES' order),
//   then x + "b" vs x + "a" and "a" + x + "b" vs "a" + x + "a" (">" when x is read whole);
// - the classes of the code points outside the table: for each run of `CLASSES`
//   (std/lang/string/collate_table.velt) but the first, the code points just below and at its
//   start against "0" ("<" for a symbol; ">" for a letter, digit or script, sorted after the
//   digits).
// The expected output is Node's (`Intl.Collator("und")`, ICU 77.1) where Node and the Rust that
// velt_rt had agree, else the old Rust's, which the port follows. They differ on 2 of the
// 15 supplementary pairs, on 65 of the 154 marked ones (ICU normalizes the marks first), on
// 189 of the 1008 edge comparisons and on 1140 of the 2858 class ones (mostly unassigned code
// points, which ICU sorts after every script and velt with the symbols).

